gie Times, the name was then passed on to Austin Reynolds who collaborated with Krome & Time for the remaining Suburban Base releases.  After the hardcore boom was over, the Phuture Assassins faded into obscurity until it was reborn once again in the new millenium with just Austin himself, doing new productions in an oldskool hardcore influenced breaks style for the Warehouse Wax label.  The most recent releases have seen a minor name change to \"Phuture Assassin\".","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:7385","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":11210,"name":"Austin Reynolds"},{"active":false,"id":46994,"name":"Terry Holt"},{"active":false,"id":46995,"name":"Bernard Simon"},{"active":false,"id":89676,"name":"Dave Jay"},{"active":false,"id":653245,"name":"Reesh"}],"namevariations":["Future Assassins","Phuture Assasin","Phuture Assasins","Phuture Assassin"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/7385-Phuture-Assassins","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/871/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"871","image":"https://i.discogs.com/wzX5NVnp1l9lmy063V-Gcn-pZj1Cb-cg0c8_9sT7Kn4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:481/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTg3MS0x/NTE2OTc4ODgwLTIz/MjIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/gcdYiei-2VVNvmjTEVSrtPqkkGUHj2f_RTdZQR7Kogg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTg3MS0x/NTE2OTc4ODgwLTIz/MjIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Born: 22 May 1969 in Detroit, USA. \r\n\r\nCarl Craig is a Detroit electronic music pioneer and the founder of Planet E Communications, a platform that has supported a diverse array of international artists for over 30 years, spanning hip-hop, jazz, funk, and esoteric electronic sounds.\r\n\r\nOperating under multiple aliases—69, Paperclip People, and C2, among others—Carl has produced six albums and over 600 remixes for artists like Depeche Mode, Tori Amos, Kenny Larkin, and Kevin Saunderson. In 2008, his remix of Junior Boys’ “Like A Child” earned him a Grammy nomination. He also launched the Detroit Love event series and played a pivotal role in the city’s electronic music festival at the millennium’s turn. \r\n\r\nCarl created the “All Black Vinyl” Instagram series, which evolved into the “All Black Digital” partnership with Beatport and Qwest TV in 2022, featuring discussions with Black artists and live streams from South Africa. This partnership continued with a Black History Month DJ mix for Apple Music and educational talks at NYU and Michigan State University.\r\n\r\nIn 2020 Carl created Party/After-Party, an immersive sound and light installation that premiered at DIA:Beacon before moving to MOCA in Los Angeles, where it became part of the museum’s permanent collection. The installation was accompanied by performances featuring Carl alongside artists like Moodymann, DJ Minx, and DJ Holographic. In 2022, Carl performed his Synthesizer Ensemble at Carnegie Hall’s AFROFUTURISM Festival and at the 59th Venice Biennale to honor Stan Douglas’s work in the Canada Pavilion.\r\n\r\nIn 2024, Carl’s life and career became the subject of Desire: The Carl Craig Story, which premiered at the Tribeca Film Festival. Directed by Jean-Cosme Delaloye, the documentary features interviews with family and notable music figures, chronicling Carl’s journey from Detroit’s middle-class roots to global renown.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:871","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1706,"name":"Paperclip People"},{"id":3255,"name":"Designer Music"},{"id":3285,"name":"Piece"},{"id":3287,"name":"69"},{"id":4835,"name":"BFC"},{"id":5285,"name":"Shop"},{"id":5788,"name":"Psyche"},{"id":6883,"name":"Urban Culture"},{"id":12439,"name":"FRS"},{"id":60328,"name":"Tres Demented"},{"id":103250,"name":"Im.mortal Music"},{"id":166525,"name":"C2C4"},{"id":214808,"name":"Parametric (2)"},{"id":458153,"name":"Free (8)"},{"id":608236,"name":"C2 (4)"},{"id":1224914,"name":"Eich, Me, Son, Sche"},{"id":1808681,"name":"No Boundaries (2)"},{"id":2761443,"name":"Carls Davis"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":3496,"name":"Innerzone Orchestra"},{"active":true,"id":5280,"name":"Urban Tribe"},{"active":true,"id":26439,"name":"Incogdo"},{"active":true,"id":80686,"name":"The Detroit Experiment"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["C","C Craig","C. Craig","C.Craig","C.Graig","CC","Carl","Carl \"Psyche\" Craig","Carl 'The Maniac Braniac' Craig","Carl Craig Presents Versus","Carl Craig's","Carl Daniel Craig","Cart Craig","Craig","Craig C","E-Craig","One Carl Craig","Senor Carlos Craig","Special Agent Craig"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/871-Carl-Craig","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.carlcraig.net","http://planet-e.net","http://carlcraig.bandcamp.com","http://www.facebook.com/carlcraignet","http://www.facebook.com/carlcraigofficial","http://www.instagram.com/carlcraignet","http://linktr.ee/carlcraig","http://myspace.com/carlcraig","https://soundcloud.com/planetedetroit","http://twitter.com/carlcraignet","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Craig","http://www.youtube.com/channel/UCdPYXwCEYfZEitsLzJozQ_A"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1109988/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1109988","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"May also appear as Saba Pivot, LLC in some releases.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1109988","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1109988-Saba-Pivot-LLC","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/2402458/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2402458","image":"https://i.discogs.com/rSrJ9KgmBTJ5bS6Dq7ob0NkN-ZDLN5va145mfs1eKhc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI0MDI0/NTgtMTYzMTg4ODUw/Ni04MzIxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/2tbGmB-w3qGpb6MKbbFHERNBGqr586a39CUDGaF-q4Q/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI0MDI0/NTgtMTYzMTg4ODUw/Ni04MzIxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Electronic music label from London, UK.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2402458","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":834556,"name":"Constant Sound"},"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/2402458-Pilot-12","type":"label","urls":["https://pilotlondon.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/label/252763/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"252763","image":"https://i.discogs.com/6J1jjPC1ITA9kIjz4RGDPPnMI5iK21QslXUwTG1G57w/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:373/w:357/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI1Mjc2/My0xMzc3ODA2OTQx/LTM0NDMuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/EjgWHe5xXNGr1zMBI3TUd9hyr1OsWIxvXVo6Z898r80/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI1Mjc2/My0xMzc3ODA2OTQx/LTM0NDMuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"US electronic music label, related to [a=DJ Demigod] releases.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:252763","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/252763-System-Records-4","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/2938511/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2938511","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Design studio associated with [a=Fredrik Melby]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:2938511","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/2938511-Anti-2","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/321228/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"321228","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Sc0CGIqlBNQj8IHksHY9panAwb52y-UpOYK0iy4PeZQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:532/w:532/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMyMTIy/OC0xMzgwNjAyNzcz/LTMxMTYuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/CNliaiHQSLg8HsuTI6wspCB9-IDNzhlyJ0cUIMVj8Ns/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTMyMTIy/OC0xMzgwNjAyNzcz/LTMxMTYuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"UK-based imprint run by [a=Joy Orbison] and [a=Will Bankhead], founded in 2011.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:321228","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/321228-Hinge-Finger","type":"label","urls":["https://twitter.com/HingeFinger","https://ra.co/labels/7355"]}},"/api/discogs/label/8564/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"8564","image":"https://i.discogs.com/0p51qQl7yu78aHPwpluspjdq7WYmdsX22ICbqTwZmx0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:290/w:494/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTg1NjQt/MTEwNjE2MDg2Ni5q/cGc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/hExW0Pwa7L094PU8YNQG8kYGWa9UuhiT8lRPW5HKo9c/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTg1NjQt/MTEwNjE2MDg2Ni5q/cGc.jpeg","profile":"American hard funk, soul, and Afrobeat record label, based in Bushwick, Brooklyn, New York, U.S.A., established 2001.\n\nStarting circa 2022, the label logo may appear as \"Daptone Recording Co.\"\n\n[b]History[/b]\nMade-up of musicians and producers from the now defunct 1990s funk revival pioneer label [l=Desco Records]. The label was formed and is run by [a=Gabriel Roth] (with his alter-ego \"[a=Bosco Mann]\" doing most of the studio mix work) and [a=Neal Sugarman] (aka [a=Sugarman & Roth]). The label is home to artists such as [a=Sharon Jones], [a=The Dap-Kings], [a=Lee Fields], [a=Sugarman 3], [a=Antibalas], [a=The Mighty Imperials], and others.\n\nThe label's home is in a converted two-family home in Bushwick, Brooklyn. The label's offices occupy the upper floors, and the its analog recording studio, [l=Daptone's House of Soul], is on the ground floor.\n\n[l=Penrose Recorders] (aka Daptone West) was established in 2012 by Mann in his hometown of Riverside, California, and Daptone's imprint [l=Penrose] Records was formed in 2020 by Mann as the home for its Southern California acts.\n\n[b]Release identification[/b]\nThe majority of Daptone's 7\" singles have a generic blue record label. However, all singles are pressed in limited quantities of 1,000–2,000 copies and some in-demand titles have received a second press run with a red-colored label after the initial first pressing had sold out.\n\nMikey Post, in charge of Daptone's direct sales and distribution, has stated as of February 2019 that their releases are continuously \"in-print\":\n\"We started barcoding our records in 2009, so anything released prior to that did not include a barcode, initially (i.e., Budos I + II). However, I'm still pulling stampers from the original 'Mother' plates, so the dead-wax is no different from the first press to the stock in print today...There are very slight differences in the color of the labels throughout the years (as I print all of our labels on an offset machine with stock paper).\"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:8564","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":670408,"name":"Daptone Recording Co."},"sublabels":[{"id":2510221,"name":"D-Bo"},{"id":3027577,"name":"Daptone Authorized Dealers"},{"id":3041278,"name":"Daptone Records Web Shop"},{"id":76194,"name":"Dunham"},{"id":123738,"name":"Ever-Soul"},{"id":36363,"name":"Misty"},{"id":225672,"name":"Penrose"},{"id":4066131,"name":"Rocksteady Series"},{"id":885472,"name":"Wick Records"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/8564-Daptone-Records","type":"label","urls":["https://daptonerecords.com/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daptone_Records","https://www.facebook.com/daptonehouseofsoul/","https://www.youtube.com/c/DaptoneRecordsChannel","https://daptonerecords.bandcamp.com/","https://www.instagram.com/daptonerecords/"]}},"/api/discogs/release/10461059":{"cached":true,"release":{"artists":[{"id":null,"name":"Delta Funktionen"}],"formats":[],"genres":["Electronic"],"id":"10461059","images":[],"labels":[{"catno":"RAM-X-10","id":683631,"name":"Radio Matrix"}],"styles":["Techno","Electro"],"title":"Junior High School Excursion To The Parallel World","tracklist":["Scitilop","Welcome To Our Timezone","Torpedo","Warp Drive","Frison",